  "question_origin": "researcher_constructed",
  "question_text": "Tavora has a civilian noninstitutional adult population of 500,000. Of these adults, 320,000 are employed, 20,000 are not working but actively looking for work, and 160,000 are neither working nor actively looking for work. The natural unemployment rate is 4%.\n\n(a) Calculate the size of the labor force and the labor-force participation rate. Show your work.\n\n(b) Calculate the actual unemployment rate. Show your work.\n\n(c) Now suppose 5,000 previously unemployed adults stop actively looking for work and no other labor-market status changes. Calculate the new unemployment rate and explain why the measured rate changes.\n\n(d) Before the change in part (c), draw a production possibilities curve for consumer goods and capital goods and mark a point consistent with recessionary unemployment.",
